data.hypothesis:
With an exact forward model and known Gaussian noise, the bounded log-k LM MLE (3 starts, 30 iterations) on all 750 validation samples satisfies four predictions:
(i) rel_l2 at or below 1.15× the CRB floor; treating the 32-draw floor as an interval, rel_l2 < 0.0232;
(ii) on the interior stratum (all true k_i more than 3 GN std from a bound), per-parameter relative RMSE within ±15% of the per-parameter CRB rel std (k1 0.0223, k2 0.0062, k3 0.0051, k4 0.0179);
(iii) mean chi^2/dof in [0.98, 1.01];
(iv) start-agreement rate ≥ 99%, with fewer than 1% of samples having per-sample relative error > 0.2.

data.falsifiable_test:
The test uses all 750 val samples with a bootstrap 95% CI. The hypothesis is falsified if any of five conditions holds:
(a) the CI lower bound on rel_l2 exceeds 0.0232, or exceeds 1.15 × the per-sample CRB if that is provided;
(b) on the interior stratum, any parameter's relative-RMSE / CRB ratio has a CI that excludes [0.85, 1.15];
(c) mean chi^2/dof falls outside [0.98, 1.01];
(d) the start-agreement rate is below 99%;
(e) more than 1% of samples have per-sample relative error > 0.2.
The fraction of estimates at each bound is also reported.

The test pairs this arm with P-009 on the identical 750 val samples using a paired bootstrap. The hypothesis is falsified if any of four conditions holds:
(a) the CI on rel_l2(P-010) − rel_l2(P-009) has an upper end above +0.001;
(b) more than 1% of samples have per-sample relative error > 0.2;
(c) initializer-only rel_l2 exceeds 0.2, if it is logged;
(d) the forward-call ratio to P-009 exceeds 0.35.

data.hypothesis:
The setup uses an identical solver (log, 3 starts, 30 iterations) on the identical 750 val samples, with only the estimator varied (posterior_mean with 512 IS samples vs P-009's mode). Four predictions:
(i) the relative rel_l2 improvement lies in [0%, 3%];
(ii) if the improvement CI excludes 0, at least 70% of the reduction in total squared error comes from the near-bound stratum (any true k_i within 2 per-sample GN std of a bound);
(iii) the interior-stratum paired MSE difference has a CI containing 0;
(iv) median ESS is at least 150 of 512.

data.falsifiable_test:
The test pairs this arm with P-009 on the same 750 samples and seed, using a paired bootstrap of the per-sample squared-error difference. The MDE is pre-registered as the CI half-width. The hypothesis is falsified if any of three conditions holds:
(a) the improvement CI lies entirely outside [0%, 3%];
(b) the total-improvement CI excludes 0 but the near-bound share is below 70%;
(c) the interior-stratum CI excludes 0.
If the MDE exceeds 1%, the outcome is reported as inconclusive at that MDE. The ESS distribution (fractions below 100 and below 50) is reported.

data.hypothesis:
The log-k landscape is effectively unimodal on [0.5, 2]^4 at sigma = 1e-3. One bounded LM run from the prior centre (multistart = 1, 30 iterations, mode estimator) therefore gives four results on the 750 val samples:
(i) a paired rel_l2 difference against P-009 with 95% CI inside [-0.001, +0.001];
(ii) fewer than 1% of samples with per-sample relative error > 0.2;
(iii) mean chi^2/dof in [0.98, 1.01];
(iv) about 1/3 of P-009's forward calls.

data.falsifiable_test:
The test pairs this arm with P-009 on the same 750 samples using a paired bootstrap. The hypothesis is falsified if any of three conditions holds:
(a) the upper CI on the rel_l2 difference exceeds +0.001;
(b) more than 1% of samples have per-sample relative error > 0.2;
(c) mean chi^2/dof exceeds 1.01, which would indicate local minima.
Any failures are inspected for clustering at corners of the box.

